Bugfix: Resolve file cache entries without mimetype without a lookup

The file cache stores an unknown mimetype as -1, and the mimetype part of such
an entry is -1 as well or, for older entries, 0. No mimetype has an id below 1,
but the mimetype loader still asked the memory cache and the database for these
ids on every call. A folder listing therefore cost two memory cache reads and
two database queries per entry without mimetype. Ids below 1 now resolve to no
mimetype right away.
